1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,578
The ruins of a town lie buried under the

2
00:00:02,588 --> 00:00:04,214
sand dunes of Lake Michigan.

3
00:00:04,764 --> 00:00:06,075
It was called Singapore.

4
00:00:06,305 --> 00:00:08,669
New York land speculators founded it in

5
00:00:08,679 --> 00:00:11,986
the 1830s, hoping it would rival Chicago

6
00:00:11,996 --> 00:00:12,882
or Milwaukee.

7
00:00:13,332 --> 00:00:16,862
After the Great Chicago Fire of 1871, its

8
00:00:16,872 --> 00:00:18,516
lumber helped rebuild the city.

9
00:00:18,966 --> 00:00:20,672
But the forests around it had been

10
00:00:20,682 --> 00:00:21,084
clear-cut.

11
00:00:21,314 --> 00:00:24,903
In 1875, the main mill was taken apart and

12
00:00:24,913 --> 00:00:26,013
shipped north to St.

13
00:00:26,243 --> 00:00:26,874
Ignace.

14
00:00:27,324 --> 00:00:28,204
People left.

15
00:00:28,434 --> 00:00:30,461
Some buildings were moved to Saugatuck.

16
00:00:30,691 --> 00:00:31,894
And the sand moved in.

17
00:00:32,544 --> 00:00:35,234
Legend says one man refused to leave,

18
00:00:35,244 --> 00:00:37,150
climbing in and out through an upstairs

19
00:00:37,160 --> 00:00:39,294
window until the sand reached the roof.

20
00:00:39,944 --> 00:00:42,441
Today, a state historical marker in

21
00:00:42,451 --> 00:00:44,688
Saugatuck says the site of the town lies

22
00:00:44,698 --> 00:00:47,039
beneath the sands, near the mouth of the

23
00:00:47,049 --> 00:00:48,107
Kalamazoo River.

24
00:00:48,557 --> 00:00:50,600
Comment your town, and it could be next.

